  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Sikorsky Aircraft has $2.8B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Sikorsky Aircraft has received 10,314 awards so far in the fiscal year and the average award size is $276K. Obligations fell 41.1% year over year. Historical obligations show variation: FY21 was $4.9B, FY22 was $3.4B, FY23 was $5.3B, FY24 was $4.8B, FY25 was $4.8B, and FY26 is $2.8B. The Department of Defense obligated $2.8B in FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $62.1M and the Department of Justice with $8.2M. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market for Sikorsky Aircraft at $2.5B in FY2026 to date. Other significant markets include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $279M and Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $20M. Smaller FY2026 markets include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $19.7M and Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing at $19.1M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did Sikorsky Aircraft's FY2026 obligations compare to prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "Sikorsky Aircraft obligated $2.8B in FY2026 to date. Sikorsky Aircraft's FY26 obligations are lower than FY25 and FY24, both $4.8B, and lower than FY23 at $5.3B and FY21 at $4.9B. Sikorsky Aircraft's FY22 obligations were $3.4B, which is higher than FY26."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Sikorsky Aircraft's biggest government customers and markets in FY2026?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $2.8B in FY2026 to date. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market at $2.5B, followed by Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $279M and Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $20M."
      }
    ]
  },
